syntax: zsh's lone `;`, and short forms ended by an operator or a comment

zsh's lexer turns a `;` that does not end a command into the same
separator token as a newline, so a lone `;` may stand wherever a
newline may: in any list, including the condition of "if", "while" and
"until", after `&&`, `||`, `|` and `|&`, and around the items of a case
clause. `a; ; b`, `; a`, `{ ; }`, `a & ; b`, `a && ; b` and
`case x ; in ; a) b;; ; esac` all parse, and `while a; ; b` is a loop
whose condition is both a and b, which run in turn on every iteration.
`;;` and the other case operators stay errors outside a case clause.

zsh also reads the list after "if", "elif", "while" or "until" only up
to a token that cannot start a command. When that is `|`, `|&`, `&&`
or `||`, the clause takes the short form with an empty body and becomes
the left-hand side of the operator:

	while a; | b    # runs: while a; do; done | b
	if a; && b      # runs: if a; then; fi && b

zsh 5.9 runs these as written in the comments: the condition of the
loop writes to the pipe until it fails, and b runs after the empty if.
`&`, and `|` or `|&` at the end of the input, stay errors, as in zsh.
`&&` and `||` at the end of the input, which zsh accepts, are a
separate change.

Last, a comment ends the word list of "for" and "select" even at the
end of the input without a trailing newline, as zsh's lexer ends a
comment with a newline token there too: `for i in a b # c`.

Reproducer, before this change:

	$ printf 'while a; | b\n' | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:10: `|` can only immediately follow a statement
	$ printf 'while a; ; b\n' | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:10: `;` can only immediately follow a statement
	$ printf 'for i in a # c' | shfmt -ln zsh
	<standard input>:1:1: `for foo in words` must be followed by `;` or a newline

With LangZsh, statement lists, the operators above and case clauses
now skip any number of `;` and newlines where they skip a newline, a
condition list ends before `|`, `|&`,
`&&` and `||`, and the parser remembers whether the input ended inside
a comment. The printer needs no change.

Part of https://github.com/mvdan/sh/issues/120.

